id: text/parse-surrogate/0001
area: text
op: JSON parse a lone surrogate
in: str:"\"\\ud800\""
out: value: str:"\uD800"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: JSON.parse refuses a string whose escape is a lone surrogate with SyntaxError, where the string holds that one code unit. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, SJL-5.5 (the text area's record; the correspondence's row J2).
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-json.parse ref:textref@1
script: JSON.parse("\"\\ud800\"")
since: 10

id: text/parse-surrogate/0002
area: text
op: JSON parse a lone surrogate
in: str:"\"\uD800\""
out: value: str:"\uD800"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: JSON.parse of a text holding a lone surrogate lets the .NET ArgumentException of its transcoding to UTF-8 escape the engine, where the string holds that one code unit. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, SJL-5.5 (the text area's record; the correspondence's row J3).
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-json.parse ref:textref@1
script: JSON.parse("\"\uD800\"")
since: 10

